sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Organizer as Organizer
    participant Flutter as Flutter Client
    participant API as API / MeetingsController
    participant App as Application Command Handler
    participant Db as IApplicationDbContext
    participant Media as IMeetingMediaService
    participant JitsiAdapter as Infrastructure: JitsiMeetingMediaService
    participant Jitsi as Jitsi Media Layer
    participant Hub as SignalR MeetingHub

    Note over Flutter,App: Flutter and API use provider-neutral API contracts only.
    Organizer->>Flutter: Start scheduled meeting
    Flutter->>API: POST /v1/meetings/{id}/start
    API->>App: StartMeetingCommand
    App->>Db: Load meeting and authorize organizer
    Db-->>App: Meeting
    App->>Media: StartMeetingAsync(StartMeetingMediaRequest)
    Note over Media,JitsiAdapter: Dependency injection resolves the Application interface.
    Media->>JitsiAdapter: Provider-neutral request
    JitsiAdapter->>Jitsi: Create / start provider session
    Jitsi-->>JitsiAdapter: Provider session response
    JitsiAdapter-->>Media: MeetingMediaSession (opaque reference)
    Media-->>App: MeetingMediaSession
    App->>Db: Mark meeting Live and save MediaSessionReference
    App->>Hub: Publish MeetingStarted event
    App-->>API: StartMeetingResult
    API-->>Flutter: 200 Result{data}
    Hub-->>Flutter: meetingStarted

    actor Attendee as Attendee
    Attendee->>Flutter: Join meeting
    Flutter->>API: POST /v1/meetings/{id}/join
    API->>App: JoinMeetingCommand
    App->>Db: Authorize participant and load meeting
    Db-->>App: Meeting + participant
    App->>Media: JoinParticipantAsync(JoinMeetingParticipantRequest)
    Media->>JitsiAdapter: Provider-neutral request
    JitsiAdapter->>Jitsi: Create join authorization
    Jitsi-->>JitsiAdapter: Provider launch information
    JitsiAdapter-->>Media: JoinMeetingResult (opaque launch contract)
    Media-->>App: JoinMeetingResult
    App->>Db: Record participant join
    App-->>API: JoinMeetingResult
    API-->>Flutter: 200 Result{data.mediaLaunchUrl}
    Note over Flutter: Flutter launches a generic media experience. It has no Jitsi SDK/API dependency.

    Organizer->>Flutter: Start recording
    Flutter->>API: POST /v1/meetings/{id}/recording/start
    API->>App: StartMeetingRecordingCommand
    App->>Media: StartRecordingAsync(StartRecordingRequest)
    Media->>JitsiAdapter: Provider-neutral request
    JitsiAdapter->>Jitsi: Start recording
    Jitsi-->>JitsiAdapter: Recording reference
    JitsiAdapter-->>Media: RecordingResult
    Media-->>App: RecordingResult
    App->>Db: Create or update MeetingRecording
    App-->>API: Recording status
    API-->>Flutter: 200 Result{data}

    Organizer->>Flutter: End meeting
    Flutter->>API: POST /v1/meetings/{id}/end
    API->>App: EndMeetingCommand
    App->>Media: EndMeetingAsync(EndMeetingMediaRequest)
    Media->>JitsiAdapter: Provider-neutral request
    JitsiAdapter->>Jitsi: End provider session
    Jitsi-->>JitsiAdapter: Ended
    JitsiAdapter-->>Media: EndMeetingResult
    Media-->>App: EndMeetingResult
    App->>Db: Mark meeting Ended and participant exits
    App->>Hub: Publish MeetingEnded event
    App-->>API: EndMeetingResult
    API-->>Flutter: 200 Result{data}
    Hub-->>Flutter: meetingEnded

    Note over JitsiAdapter,Jitsi: Only Infrastructure contains direct Jitsi SDK/API calls.
